"]},{"a":[],"id":"gcp.firestore.ttl","l":"full","t":"Time-to-live (TTL) policies","x":["Expiry is checked lazily — on the next access to the owning database — rather than by a continuously running background process; real Firestore's own TTL sweep is likewise best-effort and not immediate, so the functional difference is only in timing, not outcome."]},{"a":[],"id":"gcp.firestore.security-rules","l":"limited","t":"Security rules (editor, rulesets/releases, enforcement)","x":["Published rules are really enforced for client-SDK style requests: a Firebase ID token (Bearer JWT, issued by securetoken.google.com/<project> — decoded but its signature is NOT verified, as in the Firebase emulator) or an API-key-only request (?key= / X-Goog-Api-Key, evaluated unauthenticated). Admin SDK / gcloud / the console's data viewer / `Bearer owner` bypass rules exactly like Google Cloud. A database with no published rules denies every client request."]},{"a":[],"id":"gcp.datastore.entities","l":"limited","t":"Datastore mode entities (Cloud Datastore API)","x":["Entities, keys (ids, names, ancestors, namespaces), insert/update/upsert/delete with versions + baseVersion, transactions (all-or-nothing commit), lookup, runQuery (filters, ordering, limit/offset/cursors, projections, keys-only), a GQL SELECT subset, and COUNT/SUM/AVG aggregations are real and conform to the Datastore REST wire."]},{"a":[],"id":"gcp.datastore.indexes","l":"full","t":"Datastore composite indexes","x":[]},{"a":[],"id":"gcp.firestore.import-export","l":"full","t":"Import / Export (exportDocuments / importDocuments)","x":["Export really writes a Cloud Storage object (via Vyomi's own GCS simulator) and import really reads it back, but the file is a Vyomi-internal JSON snapshot, not the real protobuf/LevelDB export layout — the object isn't portable to a real `gcloud firestore import`."]},{"a":[],"id":"gcp.firestore.backups","l":"limited","t":"Backup schedules and backups","x":["Creating a backup schedule is real and immediately takes one backup (there is no background scheduler in Vyomi to fire later ticks on the daily/weekly recurrence)."]},{"a":[],"id":"gcp.firestore.point-in-time-recovery","l":"limited","t":"Point-in-time recovery (PITR)","x":["While enabled, Vyomi keeps a per-document version history and `documents.get` / `documents.list` / `:runQuery` / `:batchGet` honor a `readTime` in the past, really returning the document as it was at that time."]},{"a":[],"id":"gcp.firestore.insights","l":"limited","t":"Insights (query and index usage recommendations)","x":["Index recommendations and \"unused indexes\" are derived from real activity the core records as it happens (a `:runQuery`/`findNearest` that actually fails with FAILED_PRECONDITION for a missing index, and which composite/vector indexes a query's real filter/orderBy/vector fields actually overlap) — never synthetic or randomly generated data."]},{"a":[],"id":"gcp.firestore.usage","l":"limited","t":"Usage dashboard (reads/writes/deletes/storage charts)","x":["Vyomi meters real running totals (reads, writes, deletes, current document count and an estimated storage size) via a dedicated `:usage` endpoint, but keeps no history, so it cannot render the real console's over-time charts built from Cloud Monitoring metrics."]},{"a":[],"id":"gcp.firestore.key-visualizer","l":"limited","t":"Key Visualizer","x":["The heatmap is built from real per-document access counts the core records on every read/write/delete/query match, bucketed by collection and a hash of the document key — never synthetic or randomly generated data."]}],"id":"firestore","ops":40,"registry_unreachable":[],"title":"Firestore","total":56}
